{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I sent</b> — I killed your young men, and your horses were taken captive." "<b>with fire in your camps</b> — in the anger of those passing by." "<b>and in your anger</b> — those remaining from them."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Reading באפכם literally as 'in your anger'; Ibn Ezra appears to gloss it as referring to the anger of the survivors, though the passage is compressed and the antecedent of 'them' is not made explicit."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:01.624849907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}